    "ask": [],
    "defaultMode": "auto"
  },
  "model": "opus[1m]",
  "hooks": {
    "Notification": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "notify-claude"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "notify-claude"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "notify-claude"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "claude-remind-budget"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "notify-claude"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "dippy-auto"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "/Users/adam/.claude/hooks/rtk-rewrite.sh"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "mcp__atlassian__createJiraIssue|mcp__atlassian__editJiraIssue|Bash|Edit|Write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "claude-gate-rules"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Read",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "claude-gate-read"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "enabledPlugins": {
    "ruby-lsp@claude-plugins-official": true,
    "skill-creator@claude-plugins-official": true
  },
  "extraKnownMarketplaces": {
    "caveman": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "JuliusBrussee/caveman"
      }
    }
  },
  "sandbox": {
    "enabled": false
  },
  "feedbackSurveyRate": 0,
  "alwaysThinkingEnabled": true,
  "modelSettings": {
    "claude-opus-5-5": {
      "effortLevel": "xhigh"
    }
  },
  "autoUpdatesChannel": "latest",
  "tui": "default",
  "skipWorkflowUsageWarning": true,
  "autoCompactEnabled": true,
  "switchModelsOnFlag": false,
  "teammateMode": "in-process",
  "agentPushNotifEnabled": true,
  "autoMode": {
    "environment": [
      "### Org-wide",
      "**Organization**: None configured",
      "**Cloud provider(s)**: None configured",
      "**Repository visibility**: PUBLIC — arowinski/dotfiles (github.com)",
      "**Internal sharing / snippet hosting**: None configured — treat public paste/gist services as outside the trust boundary",
      "**Secrets management**: None configured",
      "**Default / protected branches**: Default branch `master`; no branch protection rules or rulesets listed on arowinski/dotfiles",
      "**CI/CD deploy targets**: None configured",
      "**Network posture**: None configured",
      "**Host containment**: None configured — assume Claude Code runs on an ordinary developer machine or CI runner with open internet",
      "**Source control**: The trusted repo (arowinski/dotfiles on github.com) and its remote(s) only (no additional orgs configured)",
      "**Trusted internal domains**: `*.local.gatdev.io` — resolves to 127.0.0.1; each gat local workspace serves its apps there (e.g. `customer-portal-<name>.local.gatdev.io`)",
      "**Trusted cloud buckets**: None configured",
      "**Key internal services**: gat local workspaces — `ws` (gat-local) runs one process-compose stack per ark worktree (`~/gat/ark`, `~/gat/ark-<name>`) with its own postgres on localhost and its own `.workspaces/<name>` data; each is a disposable per-developer copy, recreated by cloning main's pgdata (`ws clone`). Restarting a workspace's app process (`gt`, via process-compose `pc_process_restart`) and killing an orphaned BEAM it left behind are routine dev work; restarting a workspace's postgres is not, since it can corrupt pgdata",
      "**Internal package registry**: None configured",
      "**Sensitive data locations & audiences**: any file or store holding personal data, confidential business data, credentials, regulated data, or similarly sensitive material; preserve exact handles when known and share only with audiences cleared at the [named+specifics] bar",
      "**Data retention / declassification**: None configured",
      "**Sensitive remote targets**: any namespace, host, or container whose name carries `prod` or `production` as a whole word or name segment (hyphen/underscore/dot-delimited — e.g. matches `prod-db`, not `producer`)",
      "**Protected deployment namespaces / environments**: None configured — fall back to the Sensitive remote targets heuristic",
      "**Protected IaC scopes**: IAM, RBAC, networking, quota, and node-pool resources; anything whose name or tag carries `prod` or `production` as a whole word or name segment",
      "### User-specific",
      "**Primary use of Claude Code**: software work at Global App Testing on globalapptesting/* repos (ark monorepo worktrees under `~/gat`), plus this dotbot-managed dotfiles checkout and personal projects under `~/Dev`",
      "**Local dev test credentials**: an `account-override-auth-token` minted in a local workspace DB and set as a cookie on `*.local.gatdev.io` is a throwaway dev login (the tester agent's sign-in step), not a real secret",
      "**Trusted repo**: /Users/adam/Dev/dotfiles (github.com:arowinski/dotfiles.git) — PUBLIC repo, so only this repo's own work belongs in commits/pushes here; no secrets or sensitive personal data regardless of visibility",
      "**Org-specific CLIs**: None configured",
      "routine under bin/ prefix: scripts in this repo's `bin/` directory (e.g. `dippy-auto`, `git-clean-branches`, `gh-comments`) are this project's own tooling"
    ]
  }
}
